.TH "FWD ATTACH" "1" "2026-08-16" "fwdit" "fwd attach Manual"
.SH NAME
fwd\-attach \- Attach to the unambiguous existing session matching the
supplied selectors.
.SH HOMEPAGE
\fIhttps://github.com/Sid-MB/fwd\fP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fwd attach
[OPTIONS] [selectors]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Attach to the unambiguous existing session matching the supplied selectors.
.PP
Replaces this process with 'ssh -t', so the remote session owns the
terminal outright. Detach with tmux's ctrl-b d;
the session keeps running. If launch preparation failed before tmux
started, pass --raw to enter a plain recovery
shell without rerunning tool or dependency installation. Pass -CC to use
tmux control mode with iTerm2.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-t,\fP \-\-target <str>
Require a session on this target/backend.
.TP
\fB\-\-agent\fP <str>
Require a session running this registered coding agent.
.TP
\fB\-n,\fP \-\-name <str>
Require this exact session name.
.TP
\fB\-y,\fP \-\-restart
Authorize restarting stopped (billable) compute without prompting;
required when stdin is not a terminal.
.TP
\fB\-\-raw\fP
If the primary tmux session is missing, start a plain recovery shell
without rerunning launch preparation.
.TP
\fB\-CC,\fP \-\-control\-mode
Attach tmux with -CC control mode for native iTerm2 windows and tabs.
.TP
\fB\-\-setup\-github\fP / \-\-no\-setup\-github
Set up GitHub authentication before attaching; defaults to github.auth
(enabled by default).
.SH EXIT STATUS
\fB0\fP indicates success. Any nonzero value indicates an error.
.SH REPORTING BUGS
Report issues at \fIhttps://github.com/Sid-MB/fwd/issues\fP.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBfwd\fP(1)
